copy("README.md","# Closed exec gate cleanup ordering\n\nThe original Linux repository-truth run at commit 1a7afcdb820b051d1e4bfde3d436f96fc050c487 failed the post-fork identity-error control: the collector wrapper returned 125, while the actual gated root was reaped with -15 instead of its own gate-refusal exit 125. The original suite reported 13 passes and one failure. The retained [failure extract](original-failure-extract.json) identifies the immutable complete log and exact lines; it is not a replacement for the coordinator's full raw receipt.\n\nClosing the gate writer makes EOF available. The child still needs scheduling to read it and exit. The parent's first cleanup pass previously sent SIGTERM immediately, so it could overtake that refusal. The fix records successful closure of the parent gate writer and defers only SIGTERM to this exact never-released root. Its original SIGKILL escalation remains at the lesser of 250 ms and half the original cleanup grace. Total cleanup grace, absolute deadline, all descendant signals, released-root signals and actual wait4 status remain unchanged. A writer close that failed does not establish the deferral condition.\n\nThe [patch](source-and-tests.patch) changes only this ordering and adds two deterministic signal-boundary controls. The new controls use a fixed clock and signal recorder to force the race window and exact original escalation boundary. They are not native process execution observations. The [preservation proof](original14-source-ast-proof.json) shows all 14 original test methods retain identical source and AST.\n\nOnly syntax compilation and preflight were performed when this component was committed. The original Linux suite, now 16 methods, and the complete repository-truth lane remain for coordinator execution. No Linux pass, resource billing, production activation or four-second confirmation result is claimed here. The first Mac preflight used an older default Python without tomllib; its failure is retained. The same original preflight succeeded using the already installed Homebrew Python, without dependency installation or source changes to the gate.\n\nThe sole development plan and global corpus are maintained by the coordinator. This record grants no new execution, retry, payment or cleanup authority.\n".encode())
rows=[]
for f in sorted(D.iterdir()):
 r=f.read_bytes();rows.append({"path":f.name,"bytes":len(r),"sha256":hashlib.sha256(r).hexdigest()})
copy("EVIDENCE_INDEX.json",(json.dumps({"schema":"trnm-M4-component-evidence-index-v1","base":H,"files":rows,"linux_execution_included":False},indent=2)+"\n").encode())
